WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.220
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.320 --> 00:01.640
- Do you want me there with you?

3
00:02.440 --> 00:03.520
- Come.

4
00:04.640 --> 00:07.000
- Aren’t you sad at all?

5
00:07.600 --> 00:09.120
- I saw Dad with another woman.

6
00:09.600 --> 00:13.840
- The truth is, our relationship is a lie, too.

7
00:14.840 --> 00:16.040
- Are you breaking up with me?

8
00:18.000 --> 00:19.680
- Dad taught me love.

9
00:20.160 --> 00:21.680
- We just have to choose…

10
00:21.680 --> 00:24.280
- whether to drown in guilt over the past

11
00:25.080 --> 00:27.040
- or find the courage to right our wrongs.

12
02:12.280 --> 02:13.120
Hold on.

13
02:13.840 --> 02:14.520
What are you doing?

14
02:15.680 --> 02:17.040
Making steak. Why?

15
02:18.880 --> 02:20.320
You don’t need oil to cook steak.

16
02:23.760 --> 02:24.600
I know.

17
02:24.960 --> 02:26.000
I don’t need you telling me that.

18
02:34.880 --> 02:36.600
It’s not cooked yet. Why are you flipping it?

19
02:36.600 --> 02:37.480
Ouch! Shit!

20
02:38.120 --> 02:40.040
Stop talking. You’re making the oil splatter everywhere.

21
02:41.320 --> 02:41.920
What?

22
02:42.640 --> 02:43.200
Me?

23
02:43.440 --> 02:44.560
What did I do?

24
02:44.920 --> 02:47.040
Yes. You’re distracting me.

25
02:48.200 --> 02:49.360
Here, let me do it.

26
02:49.480 --> 02:50.200
Don’t!

27
02:50.200 --> 02:51.480
If you want to help, do something else.

28
02:51.480 --> 02:53.120
Get some water or make a salad. Anything.

29
02:53.120 --> 02:53.760
No.

30
02:53.960 --> 02:56.120
I’ll handle the steak, and you can make the salad.

31
03:06.200 --> 03:07.320
Or we can switch.

32
03:07.320 --> 03:09.200
You make the steak.

33
03:09.200 --> 03:12.880
And I will… make the salad.

34
03:15.000 --> 03:15.960
That’s more like it.

35
03:37.560 --> 03:38.360
Nice presentation.

36
03:41.079 --> 03:42.400
Should we order something in?

37
03:42.920 --> 03:43.240
Hey.

38
03:44.200 --> 03:45.120
I didn’t say anything.

39
03:45.320 --> 03:46.120
It’s really good.

40
03:46.840 --> 03:47.680
Can you be a little more honest?

41
03:48.120 --> 03:49.079
How am I not being honest?

42
03:50.240 --> 03:53.560
Even if you poisoned the food, I’d still eat it.

43
03:53.720 --> 03:54.120
Yuck!

44
03:54.800 --> 03:55.520
Tone it down a little.

45
03:56.280 --> 03:57.079
You’re so cheesy.

46
03:57.360 --> 03:59.640
We’re having steak for lunch.

47
03:59.640 --> 04:02.240
Japanese food for dinner.

48
04:02.760 --> 04:04.640
And then late at night…

49
04:07.480 --> 04:08.480
What should we eat?

50
04:14.000 --> 04:14.880
I’m going home.

51
04:15.760 --> 04:16.200
What?

52
04:17.680 --> 04:18.680
Why the rush?

53
04:19.600 --> 04:20.399
Stay one more night.

54
04:21.120 --> 04:21.920
One more night?

55
04:22.720 --> 04:24.440
I’ve been staying here since Friday night.

56
04:24.760 --> 04:25.880
It’s Sunday afternoon already.

57
04:27.280 --> 04:28.320
Aren’t you gonna let me go home?

58
04:28.480 --> 04:29.920
Isn’t this nice?

59
04:30.440 --> 04:32.480
You’ll save on water and electricity.

60
04:34.200 --> 04:35.360
I have work tomorrow morning.

61
04:35.600 --> 04:37.680
Then I’ll just stay at your place instead.

62
04:38.720 --> 04:39.400
What’s this?

63
04:40.040 --> 04:41.880
You’re acting like you don’t have any work to do.

64
04:44.320 --> 04:45.280
Just stay here.

65
04:54.880 --> 04:55.600
Eat.

66
04:58.760 --> 05:00.280
Why don’t you move in with Dean?

67
05:01.360 --> 05:02.080
I don’t know.

68
05:03.520 --> 05:04.240
Do I have to?

69
05:04.600 --> 05:06.760
Well, I moved in with Ten.

70
05:08.880 --> 05:09.960
You and Ten are boyfriends.

71
05:13.400 --> 05:15.200
Why haven’t you talked things through with Dean?

72
05:17.400 --> 05:17.840
I don’t know.

73
05:20.640 --> 05:21.280
Why not?

74
05:22.120 --> 05:24.280
What’s the problem?

75
05:40.000 --> 05:40.880
He’s calling.

76
05:41.680 --> 05:42.159
Who?

77
05:43.080 --> 05:43.440
Mes.

78
05:52.880 --> 05:53.280
What?

79
05:53.920 --> 05:55.320
You haven’t asked Moth to be your boyfriend yet?

80
05:57.080 --> 05:59.200
Moth and I are doing fine.

81
05:59.960 --> 06:00.840
Why do I have to ask?

82
06:01.000 --> 06:02.440
You need commitment for things like this.

83
06:03.160 --> 06:04.360
Especially for someone like you.

84
06:10.520 --> 06:11.000
I think

85
06:11.880 --> 06:13.640
Moth and I are way past that boyfriend proposal stage.

86
06:16.120 --> 06:16.800
It’s not necessary.

87
06:18.360 --> 06:19.000
Damn you.

88
06:19.840 --> 06:20.880
You’re always so confident about the wrong things.

89
06:21.320 --> 06:23.040
Moth might be waiting for you to ask him.

90
06:47.280 --> 06:48.880
[WANNA EAT SPICY PORK BONE SOUP.]

91
06:53.280 --> 06:55.080
[LET’S GO THEN.]

92
06:56.920 --> 06:59.880
[INCOMING CALL — MES]

93
07:08.320 --> 07:08.680
Hello.

94
07:09.520 --> 07:10.920
I thought you wouldn’t pick up.

95
07:13.440 --> 07:14.600
Is there something you need, Mes?

96
07:16.080 --> 07:17.400
I’m going back to New York.

97
07:18.040 --> 07:19.720
(So I wanted to ask you again…)

98
07:20.240 --> 07:22.040
about the artist residency scholarship.

99
07:23.400 --> 07:23.920
Mes.

100
07:24.880 --> 07:25.560
About that—

101
07:25.560 --> 07:26.440
(Hear me out first, Moth.)

102
07:27.680 --> 07:28.560
Think it over carefully.

103
07:30.160 --> 07:31.040
Don’t turn it down just yet.

104
07:35.880 --> 07:40.520
If I’ve eve unintentionally belittled you

105
07:41.640 --> 07:43.680
or said things that made you doubt

106
07:44.280 --> 07:46.320
(your comic character illustrations,)

107
07:47.440 --> 07:48.360
(I’m sorry.)

108
07:49.800 --> 07:51.159
(I really didn’t mean to.

109
07:54.880 --> 07:56.480
But I want you to ask yourself

110
07:57.440 --> 07:59.920
(whether you really want to turn down this opportunity.)

111
08:02.400 --> 08:04.160
(This isn’t about you and me.)

112
08:05.200 --> 08:07.680
Even if you go and you’re still mad at me,

113
08:08.600 --> 08:10.200
you don’t have to see me at all.

114
08:20.560 --> 08:21.400
Why don’t you…

115
08:24.200 --> 08:25.920
talk it over with Dean first

116
08:26.320 --> 08:27.440
(and give me your answer later?)

117
08:29.400 --> 08:30.440
What do you mean by that?

118
08:31.440 --> 08:33.480
(Dean is an important person in your life, isn’t he?)

119
08:34.400 --> 08:37.360
(Of course, you should let him have a say in this.)

120
08:42.919 --> 08:45.320
Well, yes.

121
08:48.240 --> 08:53.480
I’m glad you’ve found someone you can trust with your life.

122
08:54.680 --> 08:59.200
(Honestly, I was really impressed by what he did at the exhibition that day.)

123
08:59.840 --> 09:01.120
(When he protected you.)

124
09:01.840 --> 09:02.760
How much is this piece?

125
09:03.360 --> 09:04.200
How much did you sell it for?

126
09:04.560 --> 09:05.360
I’ll pay double.

127
09:05.800 --> 09:08.120
This work deserves to be more than just

128
09:08.120 --> 09:09.760
another meaningless piece in someone’s collection.

129
09:12.480 --> 09:14.320
I can’t even imagine myself

130
09:15.240 --> 09:19.200
caring for someone or doing the things Dean does for you.

131
09:22.320 --> 09:23.080
(Trust me.)

132
09:24.680 --> 09:26.480
(Someone as sweet and special as you)

133
09:27.560 --> 09:33.080
(deserves someone as loving and caring as him.)

134
09:45.440 --> 09:46.240
[SPICY PORK BONE SOUP]

135
09:46.240 --> 09:47.160
This one’s pretty meaty.

136
09:47.640 --> 09:48.320
Easier to eat.

137
09:51.120 --> 09:51.920
You seem to really like it.

138
09:53.400 --> 09:54.440
Want me to cook this for you sometime?

139
09:55.080 --> 09:55.680
Let’s just buy it.

140
09:56.320 --> 09:57.280
You can’t even cook steak.

141
09:59.280 --> 10:00.040
Wouldn’t it be nice?

142
10:00.560 --> 10:01.760
We could spend time cooking together.

143
10:04.640 --> 10:10.440
Actually, there are other activities we could do together besides cooking.

144
10:11.840 --> 10:13.200
those activities…

145
10:13.920 --> 10:15.080
we can do anytime.

146
10:26.880 --> 10:27.960
Mes called me today.

147
10:29.840 --> 10:32.800
He said he’d write me a recommendation letter for a scholarship in New York.

148
10:34.640 --> 10:38.200
It’s a program that supports artists and even provides accommodation.

149
10:39.040 --> 10:40.320
But I’d have to stay there for a year.

150
10:41.600 --> 10:42.240
Turn him down.

151
10:43.120 --> 10:45.720
This Mes guy sure is persistent.

152
10:55.080 --> 10:55.720
Do you want to go?

153
11:02.480 --> 11:03.600
It’s a good opportunity.

154
11:05.240 --> 11:06.720
I could keep working on my character illustrations, too.

155
11:08.480 --> 11:11.040
Can you really do both at the same time?

156
11:21.760 --> 11:22.480
We can talk about it later.

157
11:35.080 --> 11:35.920
It’s Friday.

158
11:36.800 --> 11:38.120
Did someone invite you out partying?

159
11:39.920 --> 11:40.600
I don’t know.

160
11:40.600 --> 11:43.240
I haven’t gone out with those guys in ages.

161
11:44.360 --> 11:44.760
Why?

162
11:46.520 --> 11:47.200
I feel like drinking.

163
11:50.640 --> 11:51.080
Of course.

164
11:51.440 --> 11:53.040
Let me ask them.

165
12:23.840 --> 12:26.360
Judging by your face, you could use a strong drink.

166
12:34.680 --> 12:35.240
What’s wrong?

167
12:36.680 --> 12:37.240
Is it about Moth?

168
12:37.920 --> 12:38.720
Yeah, bro.

169
12:40.640 --> 12:43.360
Moth’s planning to go abroad.

170
12:44.760 --> 12:45.720
What should I do?

171
12:47.000 --> 12:51.480
If you don’t want him to go, why not tell him?

172
12:53.120 --> 12:55.080
It’s his dream. It’s what he wants.

173
12:58.840 --> 13:00.360
What right do I have to stop him?

174
13:02.880 --> 13:03.400
Listen, Dean.

175
13:04.520 --> 13:07.920
Whether you have the right is for Moth to decide.

176
13:08.280 --> 13:11.360
You just need to follow your heart.

177
13:14.160 --> 13:14.840
I’ll be right back.

178
13:21.040 --> 13:21.840
What are you guys talking about?

179
13:23.280 --> 13:24.040
Why the long faces?

180
13:28.840 --> 13:29.320
Nothing.

181
13:30.200 --> 13:31.320
Let’s head back to our table.

182
14:17.480 --> 14:19.400
Whoo-hoo!

183
14:19.800 --> 14:20.720
Careful.

184
14:20.880 --> 14:21.760
You look hot.

185
14:22.440 --> 14:23.080
Thanks.

186
14:26.920 --> 14:29.520
Hey, watch your step.

187
14:30.160 --> 14:31.000
Look at them.

188
14:34.200 --> 14:34.920
Should we head home now?

189
14:35.320 --> 14:35.680
Sure.

190
14:37.280 --> 14:37.880
Let me book a ride.

191
14:41.960 --> 14:46.080
So, what are you going to do about Mes’s offer?

192
14:50.160 --> 14:50.800
I don’t know.

193
14:52.520 --> 14:54.160
I need to think about it.

194
14:57.840 --> 14:58.800
Do you want to go?

195
15:03.080 --> 15:04.160
Be honest with yourself.

196
15:06.680 --> 15:07.440
Do you want to go?

197
15:18.520 --> 15:19.960
Honestly…

198
15:22.400 --> 15:23.280
I do

199
15:27.800 --> 15:31.680
I’m afraid I’ll regret it for the rest of my life if I don’t go.

200
15:40.000 --> 15:40.720
What about you?

201
15:42.200 --> 15:43.080
Do you want me to go?

202
15:53.600 --> 15:54.280
I think you should.

203
15:55.920 --> 15:57.000
It’s a great opportunity.

204
15:57.520 --> 16:00.240
If you decide to go, I wish you all the best.

205
16:09.760 --> 16:10.560
The ride’s here.

206
16:11.720 --> 16:12.600
Are you coming home with me tonight?

207
16:18.400 --> 16:19.120
I’d better not.

208
16:19.920 --> 16:23.600
I’ve got a headache and feel a little feverish.

209
16:24.080 --> 16:25.080
I don’t want to give you the flu.

210
16:27.520 --> 16:28.040
Fine.

211
16:29.440 --> 16:30.160
I’m heading out, then.

212
16:30.800 --> 16:31.600
I’ll walk you out.

213
16:46.040 --> 16:46.760
I’m going, then.

214
16:47.920 --> 16:50.080
Mm. See you.

215
16:57.360 --> 16:58.520
Get him home safe, sir.

216
18:18.760 --> 18:19.720
Why are you here?

217
18:20.480 --> 18:21.160
Can you not go to New York?

218
18:27.720 --> 18:28.560
What’s with you now?

219
18:36.840 --> 18:37.640
What the heck are you doing?

220
18:39.400 --> 18:40.560
Didn’t we already talk about this?

221
18:59.440 --> 19:00.400
Can you please not go?

222
19:22.080 --> 19:23.400
Just don’t go.

223
19:26.360 --> 19:27.120
Please.

224
19:34.600 --> 19:35.680
Will you stay with me?

225
19:50.360 --> 19:51.520
You’re not going to leave me, are you?

226
20:02.400 --> 20:03.240
You won’t, right?

227
20:03.720 --> 20:04.920
Let’s stay together.

228
21:20.440 --> 21:24.440
[OUT GETTING MY VISA PHOTOS AND UNIVERSITY DOCUMENTS.]

229
21:24.440 --> 21:26.080
[I HAD TO LEAVE EARLY. DIDN’T WANT TO WAKE YOU.]

230
21:26.080 --> 21:27.320
[LOCK THE DOOR ON YOUR WAY OUT.]

231
21:45.960 --> 21:50.760
I’m glad you asked me to stay,

232
21:54.720 --> 21:57.000
but I think…

233
21:59.400 --> 22:00.840
I really should go.

234
22:19.040 --> 22:21.200
I want to be true to my heart,

235
22:24.440 --> 22:27.760
and it’s telling me.

236
22:34.200 --> 22:35.920
I shouldn’t let this opportunity pass me by.

237
22:52.320 --> 22:54.200
Don’t I have a place in your heart at all?

238
23:07.120 --> 23:08.720
I’ll only be gone for a year.

239
23:11.680 --> 23:12.840
I’ll be back before you know it.

240
23:20.200 --> 23:21.400
Are you sure

241
23:25.880 --> 23:31.160
things will still be the same a year from now?

242
23:32.880 --> 23:37.160
♪ Maybe I just love you that much ♪

243
23:38.880 --> 23:43.160
♪ So I get what’s happening to us ♪

244
23:43.160 --> 23:47.440
♪ Though I want you to stay ♪

245
23:48.320 --> 23:53.920
♪ Today I have to let you walk away ♪

246
23:56.800 --> 24:01.480
♪ No matter how much I love you, It’s pointless ♪

247
24:02.400 --> 24:06.640
♪ I’ll let reality win, Though my heart protests ♪

248
24:06.640 --> 24:11.800
♪ A thousand words of love Make no difference ♪

249
24:11.800 --> 24:16.480
♪ This is where it ends ♪

250
24:31.680 --> 24:32.400
Go.

251
24:34.600 --> 24:36.200
Honestly, I’m so glad

252
24:38.800 --> 24:43.360
you’re doing what you love and following your dreams.

253
24:55.040 --> 24:56.360
I’ll be waiting for you here.

254
24:59.960 --> 25:04.560
♪ I want to hug you one more time ♪

255
25:04.560 --> 25:10.240
♪ To remind me that once upon a time♪

256
25:10.240 --> 25:12.760
♪ We met and our hearts beat in rhyme ♪

257
25:12.760 --> 25:16.000
♪ Before you leave my arms tomorrow ♪

258
25:16.000 --> 25:18.680
♪ Before the word love has nowhere to go ♪

259
25:18.680 --> 25:22.720
♪ Even if tonight’s the last time ♪

260
25:22.720 --> 25:27.480
♪ I get to say I love you ♪

261
25:41.280 --> 25:45.720
♪ Even if tonight’s the last time ♪

262
26:08.880 --> 26:09.800
[THE DOOR IS LOCKED.]

263
26:09.800 --> 26:10.800
[MHM.]

264
26:10.800 --> 26:12.240
[LET ME KNOW WHEN YOU GET HOME.]

265
26:26.800 --> 26:28.920
Cheers!

266
26:30.240 --> 26:32.120
The lights are gorgeous tonight.

267
26:33.400 --> 26:34.560
Good luck, Moth.

268
26:35.320 --> 26:37.600
If things work out for you there, just stay there.

269
26:37.600 --> 26:38.440
Don’t come back.

270
26:39.560 --> 26:41.040
That doesn’t sound much like a wish.

271
26:41.680 --> 26:42.520
You’re basically telling me to get lost.

272
26:43.720 --> 26:46.400
If you can start a new life abroad, then just stay there.

273
26:46.520 --> 26:47.600
Come on, bro.

274
26:47.720 --> 26:49.240
Don’t say that. I feel bad for Dean.

275
26:49.320 --> 26:50.320
Why would you feel bad for him?

276
26:51.040 --> 26:52.760
And seriously, what the hell?

277
26:52.760 --> 26:55.880
We’re throwing Moth a going-away party, and that jackass doesn’t even show up.

278
26:56.480 --> 26:58.440
He’s busy with work.

279
26:58.840 --> 27:00.960
Honestly, I don’t get him these days.

280
27:01.280 --> 27:02.560
He keeps turning down my invitations.

281
27:02.560 --> 27:03.520
Gosh, I’m so pissed.

282
27:18.280 --> 27:23.200
Today, Pun and I threw Moth a going-away party.

283
27:25.360 --> 27:27.760
He said he’d go partying with your friends afterward.

284
27:28.400 --> 27:33.280
Tomorrow, he’s going to Phuket to be with his parents

285
27:33.720 --> 27:35.160
before flying to New York.

286
27:40.800 --> 27:41.480
Yeah?

287
27:43.920 --> 27:44.400
Mm.

288
27:46.400 --> 27:47.440
Moth is leaving.

289
27:48.240 --> 27:49.480
Aren’t you going to see him?

290
27:51.560 --> 27:52.560
It’s better if I don’t.

291
27:54.120 --> 27:58.000
If we’re going our separate ways, we might as well start now.

292
27:59.280 --> 27:59.840
It’s for the best.

293
28:00.800 --> 28:03.800
You say you don’t want to see him, but you’re on his Instagram all day.

294
28:08.840 --> 28:12.440
Not to mention you’ve been tailing Moth all month.

295
28:12.800 --> 28:15.280
I could be on another planet and still tell how much you miss him.

296
28:15.840 --> 28:18.240
Why are you moping around like some guy in a music video?

297
28:18.680 --> 28:20.000
Just go see him and get it over with.

298
28:21.600 --> 28:24.640
I’m not seeing him because I’m trying to control myself.

299
28:26.960 --> 28:30.320
Being away from him is already driving me insane.

300
28:33.040 --> 28:39.600
What if Moth changes his mind one day and gets together with someone else?

301
28:42.520 --> 28:43.760
Don’t you know that I could f*cking die?

302
28:44.080 --> 28:44.520
Huh?

303
28:46.520 --> 28:49.320
I’m doing this to protect myself.

304
28:50.600 --> 28:51.640
To keep myself from losing my mind.

305
28:56.400 --> 28:57.720
Can you hear yourself?

306
28:58.440 --> 28:59.600
You realize how much you love Moth?

307
28:59.600 --> 29:00.120
Yes!

308
29:01.840 --> 29:04.480
I know. I admit it. I love Moth so much.

309
29:05.400 --> 29:06.640
I love him so much it’s driving me crazy.

310
29:07.240 --> 29:09.080
But what can I do, huh?

311
29:09.880 --> 29:11.000
What the f*ck can I do?

312
29:12.400 --> 29:14.440
I tried everything to stop him. Every damn thing.

313
29:14.440 --> 29:16.280
really tried it all.

314
29:19.640 --> 29:20.960
There’s nothing else I can do.

315
29:22.840 --> 29:23.840
Do you understand?

316
29:28.160 --> 29:31.720
Are you sure you’ve done everything?

317
29:33.920 --> 29:35.120
You said it yourself.

318
29:36.200 --> 29:37.520
You love him so much you’re going crazy.

319
29:38.360 --> 29:39.400
You don’t want to lose him.

320
29:40.720 --> 29:44.120
So are you sure you’ve done everything?

321
29:58.080 --> 29:58.600
Hey!

322
29:59.080 --> 29:59.840
Where are you going?

323
30:23.360 --> 30:33.280
[MANIAC]

324
30:37.320 --> 30:38.040
Hello.

325
30:38.360 --> 30:38.920
Where are you?

326
30:38.920 --> 30:39.520
(What did you say?)

327
30:40.280 --> 30:42.080
Where are you? It’s so loud. I can’t hear you.

328
30:42.080 --> 30:42.840
(I’m at the club.)

329
30:43.440 --> 30:44.080
Hello?

330
30:44.280 --> 30:45.160
I’m at the club.

331
30:46.680 --> 30:47.440
Are you coming?

332
30:47.800 --> 30:50.160
Listen. I’m sorry I disappeared.

333
30:50.520 --> 30:51.440
I can’t hear you.

334
30:51.680 --> 30:52.320
Hello?

335
30:53.960 --> 30:54.600
Did you say something?

336
30:55.120 --> 30:56.520
I was just scared I’d lose my mind.

337
30:56.680 --> 30:58.320
So I tried to disappear from your life.

338
30:59.960 --> 31:01.360
I tried, but it really didn’t work.

339
31:01.360 --> 31:03.400
(I love you so much. I’m sorry.)

340
31:05.840 --> 31:07.000
What did you just say?

341
31:08.400 --> 31:11.360
I said I’m sorry I disappeared.

342
31:12.600 --> 31:16.000
(I tried to disappear from your life, but it really didn’t work.)

343
31:17.160 --> 31:17.920
I’m sorry.

344
31:19.440 --> 31:20.800
It’s because I love you so much.

345
31:23.600 --> 31:23.920
Moth.

346
31:25.680 --> 31:26.000
Moth?

347
31:26.600 --> 31:27.240
Can you hear me?

348
31:29.160 --> 31:30.160
Damn it!

349
31:30.440 --> 31:31.840
The light’s green! Why aren’t you going?

350
31:34.600 --> 31:36.040
Hey! Where’s Moth?

351
31:36.040 --> 31:37.440
Wow, took you long enough, dude.

352
31:37.440 --> 31:39.120
Come on. Have a drink with us.

353
31:39.120 --> 31:39.720
I’m not drinking.

354
31:39.720 --> 31:40.400
Where’s Moth?

355
31:40.400 --> 31:41.240
Just have a little.

356
31:41.240 --> 31:42.160
Let go of me.

357
31:42.960 --> 31:44.080
Hey, Dean.

358
31:44.920 --> 31:45.560
Have you seen Moth?

359
31:45.760 --> 31:46.360
He left.

360
31:46.360 --> 31:48.240
He said he had to leave town tomorrow.

361
31:49.840 --> 31:50.560
Shit.

362
31:52.840 --> 31:54.280
- Ohm. - Hm?

363
31:54.520 --> 31:55.480
Scan your face.

364
31:55.880 --> 31:57.160
Face scan complete!

365
31:57.880 --> 31:59.120
What do you need my phone for, anyway?

366
31:59.920 --> 32:01.560
There’s no way Ohm has Moth’s number.

367
32:01.960 --> 32:03.160
I remember every single digit.

368
32:16.680 --> 32:17.320
Hello.

369
32:17.560 --> 32:18.640
(Hello. Where are you?)

370
32:20.600 --> 32:21.080
Dean!

371
32:22.320 --> 32:22.920
Is that you, Dean?

372
32:23.280 --> 32:24.200
Yeah. Where are you?

373
32:24.200 --> 32:25.000
(I can’t hear you.)

374
32:26.080 --> 32:26.960
(Are you at the club?)

375
32:27.160 --> 32:29.440
Yes. I thought you were here, so I came.

376
32:31.800 --> 32:33.240
I’ll tell the driver to turn around.

377
32:33.360 --> 32:33.680
No need.

378
32:33.680 --> 32:35.440
It’s too crowded here.

379
32:35.440 --> 32:36.240
Let’s talk somewhere else.

380
32:36.960 --> 32:38.000
How about my place?

381
32:38.000 --> 32:38.960
How long until you get home?

382
32:39.680 --> 32:40.840
(About an hour.)

383
32:41.080 --> 32:42.280
Then get out now.

384
32:42.280 --> 32:43.560
Send me your location. I’ll come to you.

385
32:43.560 --> 32:44.240
Now.

386
32:44.960 --> 32:46.120
Shouldn’t we just meet at home?

387
32:46.120 --> 32:46.520
No!

388
32:47.440 --> 32:48.960
I want to see you as soon as possible.

389
32:49.240 --> 32:52.480
I don’t want to waste any more time. Not even for another second.

390
33:12.280 --> 33:12.720
Hey!

391
33:13.240 --> 33:14.280
My phone

392
33:51.760 --> 33:52.920
What the hell was I thinking?

393
33:54.120 --> 33:55.160
Who would wait for me?

394
34:41.239 --> 34:42.239
Are you crazy?

395
34:43.400 --> 34:44.719
You suddenly told me to get out of the car.

396
34:45.520 --> 34:46.560
Yeah, I’m crazy because of you.

397
34:47.000 --> 34:47.840
I missed you like crazy.

398
34:48.120 --> 34:48.880
I’m crazy in love with you.

399
34:48.880 --> 34:49.600
I was going crazy wanting to see you.

400
34:49.880 --> 34:50.800
I’m crazy about everything.

401
35:03.280 --> 35:06.880
I couldn’t stand the idea of being apart from you.

402
35:08.520 --> 35:09.840
So I tried to disappear from your life.

403
35:12.480 --> 35:14.280
But I never expected it to hurt this much.

404
35:18.520 --> 35:19.400
I’m sorry.

405
35:24.720 --> 35:29.640
I’m sorry I can’t give you what you asked for,

406
35:34.960 --> 35:35.360
but…

407
35:39.000 --> 35:40.640
Can I give you my promise instead?

408
35:45.960 --> 35:54.520
I understand if you don’t want to hear it or believe my promises.

409
35:59.880 --> 36:04.360
But even if we’re apart, I’ll miss you every day,

410
36:05.160 --> 36:05.960
very hour,

411
36:08.400 --> 36:09.520
and every minute.

412
36:11.800 --> 36:13.920
I’ll miss you to my very bones until I go crazy.

413
36:17.040 --> 36:23.800
So, will you wait for me?

414
36:32.240 --> 36:36.280
All this time, I thought…

415
36:40.120 --> 36:41.600
I’d done everything I could to keep you from leaving.

416
36:48.440 --> 36:49.200
But I…

417
36:53.840 --> 36:57.560
I haven’t really tried everything.

418
37:12.920 --> 37:13.560
What are you doing?

419
37:16.240 --> 37:17.440
Asking you to be my boyfriend.

420
37:22.840 --> 37:23.280
Moth.

421
37:27.760 --> 37:28.720
Will you be my boyfriend?

422
37:32.320 --> 37:36.000
You can study wherever you want,

423
37:37.400 --> 37:40.680
but if you agree to be my boyfriend today,

424
37:43.640 --> 37:48.120
I’ll wait for you, no matter how long it takes.

425
37:51.720 --> 37:52.760
I know

426
37:54.520 --> 38:01.160
distance and time won’t change how I feel.

427
38:06.080 --> 38:06.920
So

428
38:09.640 --> 38:10.760
If we’re on the same page,

429
38:15.880 --> 38:16.920
please be my boyfriend.

430
38:20.000 --> 38:21.600
You’re already kneeling to ask me to be your boyfriend.

431
38:22.800 --> 38:24.120
What are you gonna do when it’s time to propose marriage?

432
38:24.120 --> 38:24.880
I have no idea.

433
38:25.800 --> 38:27.000
I’ll figure that out when the time comes.

434
38:27.440 --> 38:28.640
So, what’s your answer?

435
38:32.280 --> 38:35.360
After everything I just said, isn’t my answer obvious?

436
38:39.480 --> 38:40.080
Yes.

437
39:13.200 --> 39:13.600
Wait.

438
39:14.760 --> 39:15.320
But…

439
39:16.320 --> 39:17.880
I haven’t thought that far ahead to marriage yet.

440
39:19.680 --> 39:20.480
Can we…

441
39:24.400 --> 39:25.800
take it one step at a time?

442
39:28.120 --> 39:29.080
Don’t rush it.

443
39:30.640 --> 39:31.800
Who said anything about marriage?

444
39:32.840 --> 39:34.600
- You’re nuts. - What? You just did!

445
39:35.760 --> 39:36.400
No, I didn’t.

446
39:37.160 --> 39:37.640
Then who did?

447
39:38.680 --> 39:40.400
The boat? The water?

448
39:40.680 --> 39:41.200
Who?

449
39:43.360 --> 39:44.360
You maniac.

450
39:45.040 --> 39:45.720
That’s cute.

451
39:47.200 --> 39:48.440
Can you say that again?

452
39:49.240 --> 39:49.800
Maniac.

453
39:50.360 --> 39:51.360
I didn’t catch that.

454
39:51.680 --> 39:52.640
Can you say it again?

455
39:52.800 --> 39:53.480
You maniac!

456
39:53.640 --> 39:54.280
I love it when you yell at me.

457
39:54.280 --> 39:55.440
Can you say it loud and clear?

458
39:55.440 --> 39:56.160
Dean, you maniac!

459
39:56.240 --> 39:56.720
What?

460
39:56.720 --> 39:58.200
Stop being so crazy, you crazy—

461
40:09.360 --> 40:10.280
Maniac.

462
40:11.160 --> 40:11.720
I know.

463
40:12.840 --> 40:14.360
I know you love a maniac like me.

464
40:42.440 --> 40:45.760
THREE YEARS LATER

465
41:30.760 --> 41:31.720
Wow.

466
41:32.680 --> 41:34.000
You don’t burn eggs anymore.

467
41:36.320 --> 41:38.360
Well, humans are built to evolve.

468
41:42.800 --> 41:43.680
Are you making fried rice?

469
41:44.360 --> 41:44.840
Let me do it.

470
41:45.160 --> 41:47.160
It’s fine. I’ve got this.

471
41:48.440 --> 41:48.760
What?

472
41:49.760 --> 41:50.720
Are you worried it won’t taste good?

473
41:51.120 --> 41:53.640
Of course it’ll taste good. I didn’t say that.

474
41:56.720 --> 41:58.920
My boyfriend’s cooking is always delicious.

475
41:59.560 --> 41:59.880
That’s right.

476
42:01.400 --> 42:03.000
Even if it doesn’t taste good, you still have to eat it.

477
42:04.280 --> 42:05.280
Because I’m doing my best.

478
42:18.920 --> 42:23.280
How many times have I told you to wear an apron whenever you cook?

479
42:30.000 --> 42:31.240
What if you get your T-shirt dirty?

480
42:32.480 --> 42:33.640
It’s limited edition.

481
42:33.800 --> 42:35.080
It’s not easy to get.

482
42:35.760 --> 42:37.000
You can’t buy it anywhere.

483
42:37.120 --> 42:41.360
Limited edition because nobody pre-ordered it, right?

484
42:42.800 --> 42:43.480
I’m kidding.

485
42:53.600 --> 42:55.040
Hey, I’m cooking here.

486
42:56.640 --> 42:58.280
Then keep cooking.

487
43:00.040 --> 43:03.080
I’ll just use my boyfriend to recharge my energy.

488
43:04.400 --> 43:05.200
Dean!

489
43:08.000 --> 43:09.080
Go sit down and wait.

490
43:11.840 --> 43:12.720
You’re so mean.

491
43:13.560 --> 43:14.560
It’s not like I’m asking for much.

492
43:30.920 --> 43:32.240
Let’s see, Chef.

493
43:32.240 --> 43:33.240
What are you making?

494
43:33.320 --> 43:34.600
Does that look like spaghetti to you?

495
43:49.840 --> 43:51.960
Dr. Pun is opening a new branch next week.

496
43:52.120 --> 43:54.800
You promised you’d do a review.

497
43:55.120 --> 43:56.400
I’ve already scheduled the date and time.

498
43:57.920 --> 44:00.360
Sorry to trouble you, Mr. 10M Reviewer.

499
44:02.480 --> 44:03.760
It’s no trouble at all.

500
44:03.960 --> 44:05.080
Just think of him as your friend’s boyfriend.

501
44:06.080 --> 44:08.840
Don’t feel bad. He’s gotta do it for you.

502
44:09.720 --> 44:10.160
Wow.

503
44:11.120 --> 44:14.560
You’ve really leveled up since you got together with Dr. Pun.

504
44:17.280 --> 44:20.960
So this is what it feels like to see a friend start a family.

505
44:22.160 --> 44:27.200
It’s just that your kid has four legs and likes sticking her tongue out.

506
44:27.480 --> 44:28.920
- Don’t disrespect my child! - Don’t disrespect my child!

507
44:29.120 --> 44:30.240
Aw. Your child?

508
44:31.640 --> 44:33.040
Go over there.

509
44:33.040 --> 44:34.360
Bite him!

510
44:34.360 --> 44:35.040
Finish him off!

511
44:35.040 --> 44:37.080
- Get him, girl. - Take him.

512
44:37.280 --> 44:38.280
Keep your boyfriend in check.

513
44:38.760 --> 44:39.520
I will.

514
44:39.920 --> 44:41.200
Your kid keeps messing with me.

515
44:43.440 --> 44:44.400
It’s not just Dean.

516
44:45.800 --> 44:47.400
I feel that way, too.

517
44:49.040 --> 44:49.400
What?

518
44:50.320 --> 44:51.920
Seeing a friend start a family.

519
44:53.400 --> 44:54.760
There’s a couple right in front of me.

520
44:55.280 --> 44:56.760
Nope. You’re wrong.

521
45:01.440 --> 45:02.960
Fine, you’re right.

522
45:04.720 --> 45:05.720
Try to get used to it.

523
45:06.560 --> 45:10.320
I’m happy you two finally got together.

524
45:11.800 --> 45:13.080
I thought it’d happen after I died.

525
45:15.160 --> 45:17.560
Honestly, I never thought we’d get to this day.

526
45:18.560 --> 45:21.200
But what could I do? I couldn’t resist him.

527
45:22.320 --> 45:23.400
I really love him.

528
45:26.480 --> 45:27.800
Stop indulging your friend.

529
45:30.120 --> 45:30.640
Moth.

530
45:32.400 --> 45:34.240
Are you back for good this time?

531
45:35.920 --> 45:36.920
Um...

532
45:38.760 --> 45:42.040
Actually, a lot of companies have offered me jobs,

533
45:42.840 --> 45:46.000
and there are many galleries where I want to exhibit my work.

534
45:46.640 --> 45:47.400
But I’ve talked to them,

535
45:47.400 --> 45:51.480
and they said I could stay in Thailand and send them my work.

536
45:51.480 --> 45:53.720
Kind of like a hybrid arrangement.

537
45:53.960 --> 45:54.560
Yes!

538
45:55.240 --> 45:56.120
That’s perfect.

539
46:03.560 --> 46:03.920
What?

540
46:05.480 --> 46:06.400
Why are you all looking at me?

541
46:07.320 --> 46:08.400
Have you never seen a happy person before?

542
46:11.960 --> 46:13.920
Thank you for choosing me.

543
46:19.560 --> 46:20.600
I didn’t choose you.

544
46:22.520 --> 46:24.520
I just chose what’s best for me.

545
46:27.760 --> 46:31.720
We’re together, after all. I don’t want us to be apart forever.

546
46:33.880 --> 46:35.200
When I miss you,

547
46:35.920 --> 46:37.720
I want to share those little moments that other couples get to have.

548
46:38.280 --> 46:39.520
Oh, wow!

549
46:40.560 --> 46:44.120
You finally said something sweet for once.

550
46:45.600 --> 46:48.320
As if you’ve never had your own dark phase,

551
46:48.760 --> 46:49.440
Mr…

552
46:53.160 --> 46:54.400
Monsieur?

553
46:54.880 --> 46:56.120
Monsieur. Monsieur.

554
46:56.120 --> 46:57.600
Yes, Mr. Monsieur.

555
46:57.960 --> 46:58.720
Monsieur.

556
46:58.880 --> 47:00.160
Damn you!

557
47:59.840 --> 48:02.160
Thanks for coming with me to visit my mom.

558
48:03.680 --> 48:04.520
Why are you thanking me?

559
48:05.680 --> 48:06.960
I really like your mom.

560
48:08.560 --> 48:11.560
She’s sweet and a great cook.

561
48:13.520 --> 48:15.760
If you like her so much, why don’t you move here?

562
48:27.880 --> 48:30.160
Are you serious?

563
48:31.320 --> 48:31.880
I’m kidding.

564
48:33.880 --> 48:35.600
A city boy like you could never live in the countryside.

565
48:36.160 --> 48:36.760
You couldn’t.

566
48:38.280 --> 48:39.120
Think about it.

567
48:39.920 --> 48:41.280
Who exactly couldn’t live here?

568
48:42.640 --> 48:44.720
You’re more attached to city life than I am.

569
48:45.640 --> 48:49.480
Actually, I could bring my work here and stay at your mom’s house for a month.

570
48:53.600 --> 48:57.760
Well, I used to be captivated by city life,

571
49:00.360 --> 49:03.280
but now I think I’m captivated by something else.

572
49:04.240 --> 49:06.360
Please don’t finish that sentence.

573
49:06.360 --> 49:07.960
I’m completely captivated by my boyfriend.

574
49:09.360 --> 49:12.320
If my boyfriend doesn’t live here, then neither do I.

575
49:21.840 --> 49:26.440
Back then, I couldn’t even imagine myself being in a relationship.

576
49:34.520 --> 49:38.560
Thank you for coming into my life.

577
49:52.880 --> 49:54.840
I never came into your life.

578
49:56.520 --> 49:59.280
You’re the one who came into mine first.

579
50:01.520 --> 50:02.760
I’m grateful to you anyway

580
50:04.360 --> 50:07.840
for choosing to stay in my life

581
50:08.840 --> 50:15.080
when a coward like me didn’t even dare to think about love.

582
50:21.160 --> 50:21.680
Mm.

583
50:24.040 --> 50:25.600
I’m grateful to you, too,

584
50:27.040 --> 50:29.400
for making me realize that

585
50:31.240 --> 50:34.160
I deserve love, too,

586
50:36.040 --> 50:44.040
and for making me feel like someone sees my worth.

587
50:51.760 --> 50:55.600
Even though you’re not what I imagined my partner would be like.

588
50:56.040 --> 50:58.760
Wait. What?

589
50:59.280 --> 50:59.920
What’s wrong with me?

590
51:00.400 --> 51:02.280
I’m nothing like the partner you imagined at all?

591
51:02.440 --> 51:02.800
Huh?

592
51:04.240 --> 51:05.680
It’s not like you’re that different.

593
51:06.400 --> 51:09.640
I just never thought I’d end up with a maniac.

594
51:13.920 --> 51:19.040
It’s hard to believe two maniacs like us could fall in love.

595
51:20.600 --> 51:23.680
Nothing makes more sense than two maniacs like us falling in love.

596
51:24.400 --> 51:25.320
There’s no other way.
